    "typography": [
      {
        "role": "Single-family system for every text role: 14px navigation, 18px links and supporting copy, 20px interface labels, 24px card kickers, 34px introductions, 50px testimonial statements and arrows, 80px display headlines, and 480px decorative glyph-scale type. Keeping all weights at 400 makes scale and the font's sharply calligraphic serif shapes do the hierarchy work rather than boldness.",
        "sizes": "14px, 18px, 20px, 24px, 34px, 50px, 80px, 480px",
        "family": "Symbol Helper",
        "weight": "400",
        "lineHeight": "1.00, 1.10, 1.18, 1.25, 1.40, 1.43",
        "substitute": "Cormorant Garamond",
        "letterSpacing": "normal",
        "fontFeatureSettings": "\"calt\", \"clig\", \"kern\", \"liga\""
      }
    ],
    "description": "Glyphs combines a white editorial canvas with oversized, high-contrast serif lettering and exposed type-design mechanics: Bézier handles, giant translucent glyphs, and application canvases remain visible rather than being hidden behind product mockups. The palette works in loud rectangular blocks—acid lime, cyan, orange, mustard, and deep cherry—while the surrounding page stays predominantly white and quietly spaced. One custom typeface spans every role, making navigation, editorial display copy, and UI annotations feel like outputs from the same font-making environment.",
    "customSections": [
      {
        "title": "Agent Prompt Guide",
        "content": "Quick Color Reference:\n- Paper: #ffffff — Page canvas, navigation surface, product-canvas interiors, and reversed text on dark feature panels\n- Blush Paper: #f7eef1 — Pale tinted card surface and soft alternate content band\n- Control Gray: #eeeeee — Neutral utility-control backgrounds\n- Mint Wash: #e9f3eb — Soft green-tinted list and skip-link surface\n- Ink: #000000 — Black utility text, compact headings, and neutral controls\n- Cherry Ink: #42242e — Deep plum feature-panel surface, large editorial headings, borders, and orange-on-cherry controls\n- Workshop Green: #1e3219 — Default editorial text, navigation text, logo mark, and linework over the white canvas\n- Acid Glyph: #9aff00 — Purchase and conversion surfaces, highlighted end-cap sections, and active outlined-action borders — the fluorescent green punctuates otherwise paper-and-ink layouts\n- Signal Orange: #f66a06 — Secondary feature panels, tutorial links, oversized decorative glyphs, and circular action controls against Cherry Ink\n- Mustard Proof: #f2ad0d — Warm feature-card surface and colored editorial emphasis\n- Cyan Blueprint: #1ad1e6 — Feature-card surface, product-canvas outlines, and vector-tool overlays; its technical blue makes the editor imagery read as live workspace material\n- Ochre Ink: #604900 — Text and small labels on lime and cyan feature surfaces\n- Burnt Ink: #4d2f1a — Text and borders on mustard feature surfaces\n- Blueprint Ink: #243f42 — Dark technical text within cyan-oriented editor and list content\n\nCreate a Paper hero with a left-aligned Workshop Green headline in Symbol Helper 400 at 80px/80px, then crop a 480px/480px decorative glyph behind black Bézier paths, circular nodes, and Cyan Blueprint guide lines.\nCreate a 10px-radius Acid Glyph testimonial panel with a Workshop Green quotation in Symbol Helper 400 at 50px/54.968px, flanked by raw rectangular black-and-white portrait crops and matching Workshop Green arrow controls.\nCreate a Cyan Blueprint technical callout card over a Paper editor canvas: 36px 99.896px 40px 40px padding, Ochre Ink kicker at 24px/30px, and Signal Orange continuation link at 18px/25.2px.\nCreate a Cherry Ink alternate feature card with 36px 40px 40px 99.896px padding, Paper body copy, and a Signal Orange Symbol Helper 400 link at 18px/25.2px."
      }
    ],
    "elevationPhilosophy": "Surfaces separate through flat color, 1px outlines, raw image cropping, and overlap—not box shadows. Product canvases read as precise boards because Cyan Blueprint borders and visible editor chrome replace elevation."
